CORE
main.c
--evaluation-order-check _ --div-by-zero-check
^\[g\.division-by-zero\.1\] line 10 division by zero in x / y: FAILURE$
^\[main\.evaluation-order\.\d+\] line 16 value of p is independent of evaluation order: FAILURE$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
has no effect on goto binaries
--
The evaluation order is fixed when goto-cc converts the program, hence
--evaluation-order-check needs to be passed to goto-cc. The arguments of f are
evaluated in an unspecified order: when p-- happens first, g divides by zero.
The read of p as an argument of g is moreover unsequenced relative to p--.
